Subject: [PATCH] rpc(v2): adapt blockchain, mempool and mining endpoints

Extract this concern so its mechanism can be reviewed and measured independently.
The original split preserved source semantics; candidate ownership corrections
are recorded below.

Original patch rationale (describes the unsplit source, not every extracted part):
Adapt ChainAndMempoolSnapshot, O(1) getblocktemplate, submitminedheader,
and batch mempool RPCs to V2 headers and v7 transactions.

Original-Commit: 789346a15d4342235e25878b24bf45aaabb1b71e
Original-Patch: v2/020
Split-Concern: rpc

Historical compilation prerequisites are tracked separately in daemon/patch-audit;
this provenance-preserving split does not imply standalone build validation.
Candidate-Repair: Generic syncutxoshardswarm/getfastsyncinfo controls now belong
to shared transport ecash/023. Retain only V2 pivot controls here; remove the
shared duplicate implementations/registrations and duplicate handler include.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Preserve native RPC adaptations, use original native GenerateBlock/getblocktemplate/submitsealedheader implementations where shared repaired function bodies conflict, and retain shared coroutine waiter safety. Keep one shared sync start/status RPC registration and add actual native pivot/reverse controls. Restore original createpsbt legacy-version assignment from malformed final hunk. Native snapshot/pinned-mining parity and shared sync-control interface mapping remain explicit adapter audit items.

Candidate-Application-Repair: Complete the inspected rejected native RPC hunks after adapter function renaming: retain original native generation/template/sealed-block implementations, one unsolved-block endpoint, native pivot-control registrations and PSBT version assignment. Earlier draft partial export is superseded; no successful validation identity was published.

Plan-v2 owner repair: C native context: preserve one-pass admission and local-origin trickle; retain native transaction/header and prefetch semantics.

(cherry picked from commit c9947dec7e043186670bcb781d37eed1750b6f14)

Canonical-Source-Commit: c9947dec7e043186670bcb781d37eed1750b6f14

Coordinator integration provenance (network403):
Resolve integration context by retaining the incoming purposeful change together with existing shared/native consumers; exact old/new patch and file inventory is retained in owner-adaptations.json. No authored purpose or removed downstream behavior restored.
Original scripted commands/hashes above are original-author provenance; modified parent/tool/catalog hashes are not claimed to reproduce this composition. Exact coordinator adaptation scripts and ordered tree proof are in composed403-network-metrics-delivery. Build/runtime/benchmarks NOT_RUN for this composition under user compile-first policy.

Coordinator prefix adapter: preserve canonical endpoint behavior at this API/feature consumer; exact source-only per-tree transformations and first-owner ledger retained in final507 delivery. No historical-prefix runtime claim.
